      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T14:49:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do stop epoll in case of only Quota exhaust.\nFor BW and OPS limit we don\u0027t because failing or telling the client to retry the IO will put pressure on N/W as well. So best way is to put back pressure on Client outstanding IO\u0027s.\n\nAvailable options for this.\nSince current QOS implementation is for nfs4 and above, setting the nfs41_session-\u003enb_slots limit(from 64) to acceptable number(32,16,8) based on number of clients which will be connecting(max_clients) and available ram of system should help.",
      "parentUuid": "d4e18347_5aca0cde",
      "revId": "2a58e3a6b13ce0fa855c4a103889801884804741",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
