      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T18:12:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Reading a little further, I really don\u0027t see anything that protectes the use of the fields updated here. When we do a SIGHUP, we don\u0027t pause in progress requests while we update, so an in process requests might access anything in the config. We either use atomic values, or lock the export mutex while we use the export config.",
      "parentUuid": "0d7613d2_8c0a3f49",
      "revId": "2a58e3a6b13ce0fa855c4a103889801884804741",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
