      "writtenOn": "2025-04-02T20:55:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, so it is locked, but a request in process that might utilize the QOS parameters, what serialization is there so the other thread doesn\u0027t get an inconsistent value?\n\nA possible answer is that the CPU does atomic read of integer values which is fine as long as only one such value is used in decision making. The problem arises if multiple values need to be updated atomically.\n\nStill, it is preferable to be explicit with atomic operations. Without them, Coverity might analyze that value is updated under lock but read without lock.",
      "parentUuid": "7d74ad82_4b51edf7",
